			<div class="content" id="post-content-2469015">
									

<p>When reading through the article, I wasn't impressed. It was all over the place, it was dragging on with unnecessary details, I was mentally giving it a neutral vote at best.</p>
<p>And those are still things I feel about the article. The real meat of the whole thing is the Another Sun story, and the article drags on far too long with references that really don't need to be there (did the Serpent's Hand really need to be brought up?) and articles that go nowhere fast.</p>
<p>But when you <em>do</em> get to the meat of the article, it's suddenly spectacular. This is a really unique concept that's brought out incredibly well, and secures a +1 from me absolutely. But it needs to be more prominent- as it is, it's awkwardly stuck as a footnote the end of a mediocre SCP. (As a side note, I'm very fond of the use of ze pronouns in the story. A small detail, but it's the little things.)</p>

