			<div class="content" id="post-content-2475225">
									

<p>I wasn't going to comment on this, since it's just a small nit-pick I have, but seeing as we're discussing the gender-less pronouns, I have to say they kind of broke the immersion for me, personally - simply put, I found it hard to believe that a hardened MTF member, made to recount the most traumatic event of his life, would have the wherewithal to do so in such a politically-correct manner. You'd think the use of preferred pronouns would be the last thing on his mind at that moment. And I remind you, this is a guy who isn't afraid to offend people, having no qualms about telling his interviewer to fuck off in <em>every single ending</em>. :)</p>
<p>If you really have your heart set on gender-less pronouns, though, might I suggest <em>they/them</em> instead of <em>ze/zir</em>? I don't know if there's a huge difference between those two sets of pronouns from a non-binary person's point-of-view, but to me at least this would feel a lot more realistic, coming from a guy like that.</p>

							</div>

								
