<p>I have a few major issues with this, some contest related, some not:</p>
<ul>
<li>The after action report&#8230; isn't. It's a CYOA thing narrated by a member of the MTF, and only resembles an AAR in that it describes actions that happened after they occured.</li>
<li>I am not a fan of the whole CYOA/Twine thingy. It opens up a new tab in my browser, the formatting is completely different from the wiki style, and it takes a good while to fully load. In short, it's incredibly immersion breaking, which is only made worse by the attempts at greater immersion through the use of second person.</li>
<li>This reminds me of the Dammerung skip, in a very bad way. It seems less like a skip and more like a tale wrapped up in a skip format.</li>
</ul>
<p>The story here is intriguing, and while I normally prioritize story over gimmicks (used here without negative connotations and for lack of a better term), in this case, the gimmicks weigh down what could have been a great article.</p>

